{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on 7d5a6160 (R4 item 1: Site token reuse).\n\n1. Accept the proposed design: one live token per repository and published ref, held in the existing ScopeIndex private durable custody, with these properties:\n   - binding-only acquire;\n   - the key holds the config identity, the repository tuple and the canonical ref;\n   - config, remote and publication checks stay fresh on every read;\n   - a durable reserved row before the provider call, then a single in-memory flight;\n   - the caps 256 keys, 32 mints, 8 waiters per key and 64 waiters in total;\n   - no remint on an ambiguous 401 or a network failure;\n   - no expiry extension;\n   - 503 when a cap is full.\n2. Interrupted mint: the plaintext never reached dap, so nobody holds it. Hold the reservation until its start plus the requested TTL plus 60 seconds. After that, allow one fresh mint. During the hold, reads return 503 with a finite reason. No operator resolution step is needed, and no key stays unavailable with no end.\n3. A known-expired ready row permits one fresh mint, as proposed. close releases only the request-local reader.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}